From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: rockchip,rv1126-rkvenc: Add RK3528

The RK3528 carries the VEPU540C successor of the RKVENC v1 encoder. It
takes the same AXI, AHB and core clocks and resets, one interrupt, a
power domain and one IOMMU.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip,rv1126-rkvenc.yaml     | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip,rv1126-rkvenc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip,rv1126-rkvenc.yaml
index 9a83ce1..66abfac 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip,rv1126-rkvenc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/rockchip,rv1126-rkvenc.yaml
@@ -12,11 +12,13 @@ maintainers:
 description:
   The RKVENC v1 encoder found in the RV1109, RV1126, RK3566 and RK3568
   encodes H.264 and HEVC from raw YUV or RGB frames. It reads and writes
-  memory through an IOMMU with two MMU instances.
+  memory through an IOMMU with two MMU instances. The RK3528 carries its
+  VEPU540C successor, behind a single MMU instance.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
+      - rockchip,rk3528-rkvenc
       - rockchip,rk3568-rkvenc
       - rockchip,rv1126-rkvenc
 
